{'description': "Final submission to Stavanger Tingrett by Anders and Berit Kristiansen, represented by Emma Hansen, against Carl Danielsen and NordicGuard Insurance AS, represented by Fredrik Larsen. It details the principal claim for rescission of property purchase (NOK 7,030,000) and compensation (up to NOK 2,748,904), plus interest, and a subsidiary claim for price reduction (up to NOK 7,766,734) and compensation (NOK 307,204), plus interest. It argues for the rescission of the settlement agreement due to breach of contract ('så snart som mulig' not met) or changed premises (concrete structure cannot be repaired as assumed). It also outlines the factual basis for property defects (annex outside boundary, construction flaws in concrete slab, unapproved walls) and invokes Avhendingsloven §§ 3-7, 3-9, 4-13, and 4-14. It includes a detailed calculation of restitution and compensation items and a proposed schedule for the main hearing.", 'significance': 'high', 'party_roles': ['Anders Kristiansen', 'Berit Kristiansen', 'Emma Hansen', 'Carl Danielsen', 'NordicGuard Insurance AS', 'Fredrik Larsen', 'Stavanger Tingrett'], 'deadlines': [], 'damages': [{'damage_id': None, 'category': 'direct_losses', 'amount': 307204, 'currency': 'NOK', 'basis': 'Lost rental income', 'supporting_evidence': [], 'file_id': None, 'email_id': None, 'party_role': 'plaintiff', 'significance': 'medium'}, {'damage_id': None, 'category': 'interest', 'amount': 112480, 'currency': 'NOK', 'basis': 'Avsavnsrente (1.6% p.a.) on purchase sum from 01.08.2019 to 21.07.2021', 'supporting_evidence': [], 'file_id': None, 'email_id': None, 'party_role': 'plaintiff', 'significance': 'medium'}], 'claims': [{'claim_id': None, 'legal_basis': 'avhendingsloven § 4-13, avhendingsloven § 4-14, avhendingsloven § 3-7, avhendingsloven § 3-9 andre punktum', 'factual_basis': "Settlement agreement of 30. March 2022 is lapsed due to Carl Danielsen and NordicGuard Insurance AS's breach of contract (failure to send application for 3 years) or significant breach of contract. Alternatively, the settlement was based on a fundamental misunderstanding (bristende forutsetninger) that the concrete construction could be repaired with a floating joist system, which expert reports now show is insufficient. Extensive property defects (annex outside property line, severe construction flaws in concrete slab, missing internal door, TEK10 deviations, illegal shed, unapproved walls) constitute a significant breach of contract, justifying rescission. High remediation costs (minimum 50% of purchase sum) and uncertainties make price reduction inadequate. Seller acted grossly negligent.", 'relief_sought': 'Principal: Rescission of property purchase (NOK 7,030,000) and compensation (up to NOK 2,748,904) plus interest. Subsidiary: Price reduction (up to NOK 7,766,734) and compensation (NOK 307,204) plus interest. Payment of legal costs.', 'strength_assessment': 'strong', 'defense': None, 'file_id': None, 'email_id': None, 'party_role': 'plaintiff', 'significance': 'medium'}], 'file_id': 'a8e6628d-77da-4d4b-b423-774c3324edb4', 'key_provisions': [], 'file_date': '2025-06-02', 'category': 'pleading'}
