{'title': 'Final Submission - Danielsen & NordicGuard Insurance', 'description': 'Final submission to Rogaland Tingrett from Danielsen and NordicGuard Insurance AS, arguing that the settlement agreement from March 2022 is valid and binding, and that they have not breached their obligations. They dispute the grounds for rescission and argue that any defects are covered by an "as is" clause, or that rescission was declared too late. They admit to some minor defects for which a price reduction might be applicable, but dispute the amount.', 'significance': 'high', 'party_roles': ['plaintiff', 'defendant', 'insurer', 'legal_rep_defendant', 'expert'], 'deadlines': [{'deadline_id': None, 'deadline_date': '2025-06-09', 'description': 'Deadline for submitting the final submission.', 'file_id': None, 'email_id': None, 'party_role': 'defense_counsel', 'significance': 'high'}], 'damages': [{'damage_id': None, 'category': 'direct_losses', 'amount': None, 'currency': None, 'basis': "Price reduction and/or compensation limited by court's discretion.", 'supporting_evidence': [], 'file_id': None, 'email_id': None, 'party_role': None, 'significance': 'medium'}], 'claims': [{'claim_id': None, 'legal_basis': 'Implied by settlement agreement', 'factual_basis': "The settlement agreement is valid and binding, and our clients have actively worked to fulfill their obligations. The application process took time due to necessary clarifications with the neighborhood association and neighbor, and there was no specific deadline for submission. 'As soon as possible' must be interpreted in light of real possibilities.", 'relief_sought': 'That the settlement agreement is upheld and the termination is withdrawn.', 'strength_assessment': 'strong', 'defense': None, 'file_id': None, 'email_id': None, 'party_role': None, 'significance': 'medium'}, {'claim_id': None, 'legal_basis': 'avhendingsloven § 4-13', 'factual_basis': "It is disputed that there are grounds for rescission. Even if there are defects, they are not of a character to constitute a material breach. Repair costs should be set at the defendant's lower estimate.", 'relief_sought': 'Carl Danielsen and NordicGuard Insurance AS be acquitted.', 'strength_assessment': 'strong', 'defense': None, 'file_id': None, 'email_id': None, 'party_role': None, 'significance': 'medium'}, {'claim_id': None, 'legal_basis': 'avhendingsloven § 4-13', 'factual_basis': 'The rescission declaration was submitted on June 21, 2021, almost two years after takeover and long after the defects were discovered, thus it was submitted too late.', 'relief_sought': 'Carl Danielsen and NordicGuard Insurance AS be acquitted.', 'strength_assessment': 'strong', 'defense': None, 'file_id': None, 'email_id': None, 'party_role': None, 'significance': 'medium'}, {'claim_id': None, 'legal_basis': 'avhendingsloven § 3-9', 'factual_basis': "Property was sold 'as is', meaning risk for hidden defects is largely transferred to the buyer.", 'relief_sought': 'Carl Danielsen and NordicGuard Insurance AS be acquitted.', 'strength_assessment': 'strong', 'defense': None, 'file_id': None, 'email_id': None, 'party_role': None, 'significance': 'medium'}, {'claim_id': None, 'legal_basis': 'avhendingsloven § 3-7', 'factual_basis': "It is denied that there was a failure to disclose information. The seller had no knowledge of the alleged conditions (property within boundary, construction of addition, unapproved walls) and answered buyer's questions to the best of their ability.", 'relief_sought': 'Carl Danielsen and NordicGuard Insurance AS be acquitted.', 'strength_assessment': 'strong', 'defense': None, 'file_id': None, 'email_id': None, 'party_role': None, 'significance': 'medium'}, {'claim_id': None, 'legal_basis': 'Implied by property defect claim', 'factual_basis': "It is disputed that the addition must be demolished and rebuilt. The defendant's expert (Konsulent Gruppen AS v/Thomas Strand) believes the deck has sufficient bearing capacity and a floating joist solution is sufficient.", 'relief_sought': 'Carl Danielsen and NordicGuard Insurance AS be acquitted.', 'strength_assessment': 'strong', 'defense': None, 'file_id': None, 'email_id': None, 'party_role': None, 'significance': 'medium'}, {'claim_id': None, 'legal_basis': 'Implied by property defect claim', 'factual_basis': 'It is disputed that the property boundary problem cannot be solved. A signed draft agreement exists with the neighbor for an exchange, and the municipality will likely approve a minor boundary adjustment.', 'relief_sought': 'Carl Danielsen and NordicGuard Insurance AS be acquitted.', 'strength_assessment': 'strong', 'defense': None, 'file_id': None, 'email_id': None, 'party_role': None, 'significance': 'medium'}, {'claim_id': None, 'legal_basis': 'avhendingsloven § 4-14', 'factual_basis': "It is disputed that there are grounds for compensation. The defects are hidden and outside the seller's control. Plaintiff's compensation claims for lost appreciation, lost rental income, and deduction for living benefits are disputed.", 'relief_sought': 'Carl Danielsen and NordicGuard Insurance AS be acquitted.', 'strength_assessment': 'strong', 'defense': None, 'file_id': None, 'email_id': None, 'party_role': None, 'significance': 'medium'}, {'claim_id': None, 'legal_basis': 'Implied by compensation claim', 'factual_basis': 'Interest for deprivation should not be awarded when compensation for lost appreciation is awarded for the same period.', 'relief_sought': 'Carl Danielsen and NordicGuard Insurance AS be acquitted or pay reduced compensation.', 'strength_assessment': 'strong', 'defense': None, 'file_id': None, 'email_id': None, 'party_role': None, 'significance': 'medium'}], 'file_id': 'e0864072-809b-49e5-9f5e-5436d4841c84', 'key_provisions': ['avhendingsloven §§ 3-7', 'avhendingsloven §§ 3-8', 'avhendingsloven §§ 3-9', 'avhendingsloven §§ 4-13', 'avhendingsloven §§ 4-14', 'avhendingsloven §§ 4-19', 'tviseloven'], 'file_date': '2025-06-06', 'category': 'pleading'}
