{'title': 'Notes from Witness Testimony: Thomas Strand', 'description': "Thomas Strand, a civil engineer from Teknisk Rådgivning AS, testified on June 25, 2025, regarding the concrete deck. His 2021 report concluded that a floating joist system is acceptable, assuming the deck is relieved and water intrusion stops. He disagreed with Betongteknikk AS's assessment that corrosion would continue. However, he admitted his assessment was based solely on documentation and could change if new information, like moisture measurements or deeper cracks, was considered.", 'significance': 'medium', 'party_roles': ['Thomas Strand', 'adv. Larsen', 'adv. Hansen', 'retten'], 'deadlines': [], 'damages': [{'damage_id': None, 'category': 'direct_losses', 'amount': 600000, 'currency': 'NOK', 'basis': "Cost for floating joist system (defendant's expert estimate)", 'supporting_evidence': [], 'file_id': None, 'email_id': None, 'party_role': None, 'significance': 'medium'}], 'claims': [{'claim_id': None, 'legal_basis': 'Implied by property defect claim', 'factual_basis': "It is disputed that the addition must be demolished and rebuilt. The defendant's expert (Konsulent Gruppen AS v/Thomas Strand) believes the deck has sufficient bearing capacity and a floating joist solution is sufficient.", 'relief_sought': 'Carl Danielsen and NordicGuard Insurance AS be acquitted.', 'strength_assessment': 'moderate', 'defense': None, 'file_id': None, 'email_id': None, 'party_role': None, 'significance': 'medium'}], 'file_id': '57f4acfb-0ff9-426a-997a-d36c9838e95b', 'key_provisions': [], 'file_date': '2025-06-25', 'category': 'witness_statement'}
