{'title': 'Report: Concrete Slab Assessment Fjellveien 42A', 'description': 'BetongTeknikk AS assesses the concrete slab above the rental unit at Fjellveien 42A, detailing water ingress, cracks, leaks, and high moisture. The report concludes that the proposed solution of a floating joist system is insufficient and strongly recommends demolition and reconstruction of the deck as the only long-term solution.', 'significance': 'high', 'party_roles': ['Anders Kristiansen', 'Berit Kristiansen', 'Thor Berntsen', 'BetongTeknikk AS'], 'deadlines': [], 'damages': [], 'claims': [], 'file_id': '7a98b693-5720-4bfe-8ec8-57d5ce3da108', 'key_provisions': ['Water ingress in mid-layer of slab, confirmed by drilling and moisture measurement.', 'Cracks (0.3 - 0.5 mm) and larger fissures observed in the underside of the slab (ceiling), particularly at mid-span.', 'Active water leakage observed at multiple points in the ceiling.', 'High moisture in elements and polyconcrete layer.', 'Water originates from a leaky membrane under the terrace tiles.', 'Consequences: continued deflection and cracking, corrosion of rebar (due to moisture, oxygen, and crack width), spalling of concrete.', 'Lack of protection: rebar is in a draining area with oxygen and moisture; support beams should have been cast between concrete layers for rust protection.', "Proposed 'floating joist system' is VERY LIMITED and will NOT prevent further deflection, cracking, corrosion, or spalling.", 'Recommendation: DEMOLITION AND RECONSTRUCTION of the deck is the only solution to remove corrosion risk, ensure compliant construction, and provide a long-term durable solution.'], 'file_date': '2023-02-24', 'category': 'expert_report'}
