{'title': 'Technical Report on Structural Assessment Fjellveien 42A', 'description': 'A technical report from Teknisk Rådgivning AS for Advokatfirmaet Nord, dated October 21, 2021. It assesses the concrete slab in the extension at Fjellveien 42A, which serves as a floor separation and terrace. The report highlights uncertainties regarding the slab\'s load-bearing capacity due to missing documentation, deviations from pre-accepted performance, and observed damages (leaks, cracks). It evaluates the proposed solution of a floating joist floor ("roof over roof") as acceptable for preventing further damage and relieving the existing structure, but notes it doesn\'t eliminate all uncertainty. Full safety would require demolition and reconstruction.', 'significance': 'high', 'party_roles': ['Advokatfirmaet Nord', 'Fredrik Larsen', 'Teknisk Rådgivning AS', 'Thomas Strand', 'K2 Taksering AS', 'Byggesøknad Stavanger AS'], 'deadlines': [], 'damages': [], 'claims': [], 'file_id': 'cdeeea87-1d4e-4600-8a58-fd5304ab02b1', 'key_provisions': ['Assessment based on documentation, no physical inspection.', 'Slab consists of plate decks, reinforcement, polyconcrete, cast concrete, membrane, tiles (approx. 200mm thick).', 'Deviations: No support beams found, 200mm vs. 250mm thickness, thinner polyconcrete, thicker cast concrete, no design documentation.', 'Uncertainty about load-bearing capacity due to lack of documentation and deviations.', 'Observed damages: leaks, cracks (not typically directional for overloading).', 'Floating joist floor ("roof over roof") solution: Pros (prevents water, relieves slab, cost-effective, avoids demolition), Cons (doesn\'t solve unknown load-bearing, existing slab remains, long-term uncertainty).', 'Floating joist floor deemed acceptable with conditions (max relief, complete waterproofing, inspection, monitoring).', 'Demolition and reconstruction preferred for full safety but costly.'], 'file_date': '2021-10-21', 'category': 'expert_report'}
